  "entry": "code/apps/demo/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Turns recorded skeleton-tracking trials (Kinect, MediaPipe or offline JSON/CSV dumps) into shoulder and hip angle asymmetry measures (RS_θ, LS_θ, Δθs, RH_θ, LH_θ, Δθh) for static standing and dynamic walking, with time-domain and STFT plots and a summary that separates healthy-like from elevated asymmetry, either for a batch of subjects or for one subject. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
